From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: Ctrl+wheel scrolls

On Aura, Chrome classifies a wheel tick with Ctrl held as kPageZoom.
MouseWheelEventQueue makes no scroll from it and WebContentsImpl hands
it to ContentsZoomChange. In Domicile the shell ignored it and a
<webview> turned it into a zoom request, so neither scrolled.

GetPlatformSpecificDefaultEventAction no longer returns kPageZoom, so
Ctrl+wheel scrolls like a plain wheel. The page still gets a `wheel`
with `ctrlKey` and can preventDefault it.

WheelActionTest in domicile_unittests checks a Ctrl+wheel tick scrolls.
---
 third_party/blink/common/input/web_mouse_wheel_event.cc | 8 ++------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/common/input/web_mouse_wheel_event.cc b/third_party/blink/common/input/web_mouse_wheel_event.cc
index 9c5ab493..d1a18d64 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/common/input/web_mouse_wheel_event.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/common/input/web_mouse_wheel_event.cc
@@ -117,12 +117,8 @@ WebMouseWheelEvent::EventAction
 WebMouseWheelEvent::GetPlatformSpecificDefaultEventAction(
     const WebMouseWheelEvent& event) {
 #if defined(USE_AURA) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
-  // Scroll events generated from the mouse wheel when the control key is held
-  // don't trigger scrolling. Instead, they may cause zooming.
-  if (event.delta_units != ui::ScrollGranularity::kScrollByPrecisePixel &&
-      (event.GetModifiers() & WebInputEvent::kControlKey)) {
-    return blink::WebMouseWheelEvent::EventAction::kPageZoom;
-  }
+  // Domicile: Ctrl+wheel scrolls. Chrome makes it kPageZoom, which no page
+  // scrolls by. The page still sees `ctrlKey` and may preventDefault.
 
   if (event.delta_x == 0 && (event.GetModifiers() & WebInputEvent::kShiftKey))
     return blink::WebMouseWheelEvent::EventAction::kScrollHorizontal;
